# SHA-1 (FIPS 180-4, Secure Hash Standard, 2015, sections 4.1.1, 4.2.1,
# 5.1.1, 5.3.1 and 6.1): a 160-bit digest of 64-byte blocks, eighty steps
# over a message schedule of eighty words (unrolled by gen/rounds.py).
# Big-endian words; the length in bits is padded in big-endian. SHA-1 is
# broken for collisions (SHAttered, 2017): it is here for HMAC-SHA-1,
# PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA-1 and the formats that require it.
#
# The hash, as the crypto package's hash interface takes it:
#   ~Hs.HsMdState<Hs.HsW5>, ~64n, ~20n, ~HsSha1.init(), ~HsSha1.update,
#   ~HsSha1.final, ~HsSha1.digest
import Base
